course: dictionary
lesson: 5249
title: Jog: one word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words wear more than one coat. Jog can be a verb (something you do) or a noun (a thing you have). Read the words around it to find which meaning fits. «Junior parkrun is a free 2 km run on Sunday mornings, and walking and jogging are welcome.» Here jogging means running slowly and steadily, the way you run for exercise.
explain: Jog can also be a noun: «go for a jog» means go for a short, slow run. The words «go for a» tell you it is a thing you can go for, like a walk. Try it: «go for a run» also makes sense, so the noun fits.
explain: «A warm-up of jogging, skips and leg swings slowly raises your heart rate.» Jogging is one of several gentle moves before sport. The clue is the warm-up: it is easy, steady movement, not a race.
explain: Jog has two other meanings. To jog something is to push or knock it a little, as in «He jogged my arm». To jog your memory is to help you remember something. When you meet jog, try each meaning in the sentence and see which one still makes sense.
fact: Jog can be a verb (jog, jogs, jogged, jogging) or a noun (a jog, jogs).
fact: «To jog» means to run slowly and steadily, often for exercise.
fact: «A jog» means a slow run, as in «go for a jog».
fact: «To jog something» means to push or knock it a little, as in «He jogged my arm».
fact: «To jog your memory» means to help you remember something.
exercise: «A few minutes of jogging and moving stretches warms the muscles up before going on.» What does jogging mean here? | Sitting very still | Pushing something a little | Shouting loudly | *Running slowly and steadily
exercise: Mum says, «Let's go for a jog around the park.» What is a jog in this sentence? | *A slow run | A large dog | A type of cake | A bump in the road
exercise: «He jogged my arm, so my pencil slipped.» What does jogged mean? | Helped me remember | *Pushed or knocked a little | Ran very fast | Stopped and sat down
test: Sam asks, «Can you jog my memory about the date of the trip?» What does jog my memory mean? | Push my head gently | Forget the date | Run around my head | *Help me remember
test: Which word can be a noun meaning a short, slow run? | Tiptoe | Dash | Jump | *Jog
exam: Which meaning of jog fits «He gave my sleeve a jog to get my attention»? | Sitting still and quiet | To run for exercise | To remember something | *To push or knock a little
